cff-version: 1.2.0
title: archeus
message: >-
  The memory and workspace layer for AI coding agents. Note that an unrelated
  Rust project also publishes under the name "archeus"; this entry describes
  the Python package at https://pypi.org/project/archeus/.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Babar Muhammad
    family-names: Anas
    website: 'https://claudectl.space'
repository-code: 'https://github.com/babarmuhammad/archeus'
url: 'https://claudectl.space'
version: 2.1.0
date-released: '2026-09-09'
abstract: >-
  A memory and workspace layer for AI coding agents, driving Anthropic's Claude
  Code CLI today. Browse, search, tag, fork and resume every session across
  every project and account; maintain a semantic project memory that is
  injected within a token budget; manage MCP servers, agents, skills and hooks;
  and see what a turn costs, read from your own transcripts. Terminal UI and
  desktop GUI over one engine, with zero runtime dependencies.
keywords:
  - ai-agents
  - agent-memory
  - coding-agent
  - context-management
  - claude-code
  - developer-tools
  - terminal-ui
  - session-manager
  - mcp
